From 6c7a635668f1ff53125d87301465a3f8db6e0ca0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 10:33:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] fix(sync): close a realtime connection made while the
 repository closes; make shared state volatile

CandySyncRepository serializes its work on one dispatcher thread, but observe(), close() and
currentState() run on the host's thread. state, the realtime fields and the listeners are now
@Volatile (the listeners a list that is replaced, not changed in place), and a connection that
finishes after close() is closed instead of staying open: close() found nothing to close.

Test: the transport closes the repository while it is connecting.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SQZTihurw1LavH7Cgs1UnR
---
